{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1353988-requesting-page-reference-for-quintessence-limit","id":1353988,"title":"Requesting page reference for Quintessence Limit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-09T16:09:13-08:00","id":1353988,"title":"Requesting page reference for Quintessence Limit","content":"My group has gotten into some pretty intense discussions about precisely how much Quintessence a mage can store within themselves. <br /> <br /> From reading this forum, I know that a mage without Prime can only store up to their Avatar rating in Quintessence and with Prime 1 a mage can store up to 20 Quintessence. I also know that the Quintessence wheel has 20 slots, and it can be inferred that one can store 20 Quintessence because of this. However, despite searching the book for literal hours by now, I haven't been able to find a page that directly states that a mage with Prime 1 can store up to 20 Quintessence within themselves. If anyone can provide a page reference for that, I'd be extremely appreciative so that my group can finally settle this discussion once-and-for-all. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25846-legitpancake","name":"LegitPancake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T16:28:41-08:00","id":1353992,"title":"","content":"There is no literal sentence like &quot;A Mage can only hold 20 points of Quintessence&quot;, but I don't know how much more clear &quot;Prime energy is tracked on the 20-box<br /> Quintessence/ Paradox wheel.&quot; can be.<br /> <br /> Now, a Mage can only store 20 quintessence. It's the max of the wheel, and more importantly: It's why Paradox eats into your stored quintessence if those two values meet.<br /> However, it is not *quite* true that a Mage can *only* hold 20 points of Quintessence *ever* - it's exactly what Periapts are for, to allow the Mage to carry more around with them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not only that, but the Paradox won't eat into them - only the Wheel.<br /> <br /> As for Prime 1 - gotta be careful there. A Mage with Prime 1 *can* hold more than their Avatar worth of Quintessence - up to those 20...but they have no means of doing that to themselves yet. They *can't* fill themselves up with more than what their Avatar can handle (By the usual using meditation at a Node).<br /> But. What Prime 1 allows is, somebody who has Prime 3 can infuse them with more Quintessence than what their Avatar can handle by itself. The target *has* to have Prime 1 for that in order for their Avatar to be aligned to handle it.<br /> But to actually do it to yourself you need Prime 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 12-09-2019, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T16:39:16-08:00","id":1353995,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your substantative answer! I suspected the 20 Quintessence maximum wasn't ever stated directly, but it's good to have someone settle it. I also appreciate you explaining how Prime 1 functions exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25846,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25846-legitpancake","user":"LegitPancake","date":". 12-09-2019, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25846-legitpancake","name":"LegitPancake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T15:41:03-08:00","id":1354255,"title":"","content":"It should also be noted that anyone with Prime 1+ also theoretically has access to the extra Quintessence contained in their own Health levels, though obviously making that conversion is an option of last resort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T21:33:05-07:00","id":1374489,"title":"","content":"Sorry to resurrect this one from a few months ago but this is wrong.<br /> <br /> QUOTE=Ambrosia;n1353992]As for Prime 1 - gotta be careful there. A Mage with Prime 1 *can* hold more than their Avatar worth of Quintessence - up to those 20...but they have no means of doing that to themselves yet. They *can't* fill themselves up with more than what their Avatar can handle (By the usual using meditation at a Node).[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> M20 Page 332<br /> Channeling Quintessence through the Avatar requires meditation at a Node; channeling more than your Avatar rating through that Node requires Prime 1. <br /> <br /> The rest of your statement is absolutely correct of course. <br /> <br /> Totaly not trying to just call you out on this but it caught my attention because we've being doing this since revised so I thought we were doing it wrong after reading your post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T23:59:12-07:00","id":1374515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1353988-requesting-page-reference-for-quintessence-limit?p=1374489#post1374489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to resurrect this one from a few months ago but this is wrong.<br /> <br /> M20 Page 332<br /> Channeling Quintessence through the Avatar requires meditation at a Node; channeling more than your Avatar rating through that Node requires Prime 1.<br /> <br /> The rest of your statement is absolutely correct of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch there!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}